  "answer": "Across the walks F1, F2, G1, G2 (CAP-U9DOUBLE-*), CAP-U9PLUS24 A and B and CAP-U9OPENWALK A and B, every frame logged: a push doubles only when the panel's move shows a frame or more after the frame's scroll (more than 18 ms). 17 pushes doubled, all late; 123 pushes moved in the frame after the scroll and none doubled; 10 late pushes were exact. Places: F 488 doubled 4 of 5 (CAP-U9DEMO F, PLUS24 A and B, F1; not F2), G 468 in G1 and G2 but not CAP-U9DEMO G, G 228 only in CAP-U9DEMO; on the open walk 896 up, 946 and 1096 down doubled in both runs, 846, 746 and 1346 in one. So a place makes it likely and the trigger is timing: inferred, a race in the oracle's page between the scroll and the panel's update. Not built: when the update lands a frame late isn't set by the page's state, so ours keeps the frozen rule, its update in the scroll's frame."
